  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "frnkdhn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Ancient History"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The ancient history of Himachal Pradesh spans the Vedic, Epic, Maurya, and Gupta periods.",
        "Medieval history comprises major regional powers such as the Katoch Dynasty of Kangra and the Chamba Kingdom.",
        "Key medieval historical phases include the Mughal Period (1556–1707 CE), Gurkha Invasion (1803–1815 CE), and Sikh Period (1809–1846 CE).",
        "During the British Period (1846–1947), Simla served as the Summer Capital of British India.",
        "Post-Independence developments trace the political formation of the state and the succession of Chief Ministers of Himachal Pradesh."
      ],
      "id": "k77ueej"
    },
